# GitHub attribution (owner only)

The repo owner (`Ogrods`) opens, merges, and publishes pull requests and GitHub Releases. Automated app identities must never appear as the publisher on those surfaces.

## Agents must not

- Open, edit metadata on, merge, close, or reopen pull requests (including forge helper UIs that create PRs under an app account).
- Create, edit, or publish GitHub Releases, or push version tags meant for release publish.
- Leave empty or no-op commits whose only purpose is to re-run CI (that attributes the workflow run to the pusher app). Report the failed check and let the owner re-run or push.

## Agents may

- Push commits to an existing branch the owner already opened a PR from.
- Push a new branch and stop. Tell the owner the branch name so **they** open the PR.
- Fix code/lockfiles on Dependabot or other bot-authored branches when asked; still do not open a second PR for the same change.

## Commit messages

Keep subjects and bodies about the product or repo change. No tooling or agent names, no "AI"/"LLM"/"bot" framing, no session diary. Prefer short imperative lines (same voice as public changelog: facts only). Do not add `Co-authored-by` trailers that name agent or editor tooling.
